  "blurb": "In a June 2026 special session called by Gov. Ron DeSantis, the Legislature put a property-tax amendment on the Nov 3 ballot as Amendment 3. It would raise the homestead exemption on non-school property taxes and limit how counties and cities use property taxes. Supporters say it puts money back in homeowners' pockets. Opponents, including city and county governments and legislative Democrats, say it shifts costs and would force cuts to local services. A constitutional amendment needs 60 percent of the vote to pass. In August 2026 a Leon County judge ordered the ballot text rewritten; the lawsuits did not ask to take the measure off the ballot. In a University of North Florida poll of 1,511 Florida homeowners (reported Sep 28, 2026), 63 percent said they were more concerned about property insurance than about property taxes.",
